{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 220,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"The Universe,\" informally, means \"everything\nthere is\" - mountains and oceans and the moon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5410,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hot nuclear balls of hydrogen and a whole\nlot more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8940,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the Universe is \"everything\", does\nthat mean it includes the things that we don't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12990,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know that we don't know exist?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15340,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or even the things that we believe exist but\nhaven't yet seen or observed?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18929,
    "dDurationMs": 3641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, is the future a part of the universe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22570,
    "dDurationMs": 4939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In physics, we usually distinguish between\nthese two notions of universe as 1) the \"observable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27509,
    "dDurationMs": 7641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe,\" which is everything whose existence\nwe've thus far been able to confirm or observe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35150,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 2) \"The Universe\" with a capital U, or,\n\"The Whole Universe,\" which is everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40090,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that exists, has existed, or will exist, any\ntime, anywhere, regardless of whether or not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44710,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're aware of it yet (or ever will be)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47120,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, the main reason for this distinction\nis so that we can talk scientifically about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50670,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parts of the universe we haven't yet been\nable to observe, and the two biggest reasons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54320,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we might not have been able to observe a piece\nof the universe yet are either it's in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58170,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "future or it's so far away that light from\nit hasn't had time to reach us - yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62890,
    "dDurationMs": 5470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To explain: as far as we know, the universe\nhad a beginning and is now around 13.8 billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68360,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years old."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69450,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light takes time to travel through space,\nso anywhere too far away from us just isn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "visible yet in the same way that thunder from\na distant lightning strike isn't audible - until"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78720,
    "dDurationMs": 1270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you wait long enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79990,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you were blind, the thunder would be the\nfirst sign you have of the storm's existence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84190,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though once you hear it, you can infer that\nthe storm must have existed all along."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88160,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So within the observable universe, what do\nwe know \"exists\"?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91580,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pretty much just three things: spacetime,\nparticles, and the physical laws that describe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96460,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how spacetime and those particles interact\nto give rise to gravity and matter and forces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100980,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and everything else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102550,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's open for debate whether or not mathematics\nis a part of the universe or if it exists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106250,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"outside\" the universe in some sort of mathematical\nheavens - but if you think that mathematics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110890,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exists and if The Universe is everything that\nexists, then, well..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115750,
    "dDurationMs": 1299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll leave that up to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117049,
    "dDurationMs": 4451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's one other thing, though - you may\nhave heard of parallel universes, or \"Multiverses,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121500,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an idea proposed by researchers or sci-fi\nfanatics that perhaps what we think of as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126460,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Universe is actually just a small piece\nof a larger thing which is really \"everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130910,
    "dDurationMs": 27630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is\"... but that's anotherverse in the\nstory."
    } ]
  } ]
}
